    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented for **version 2 of the owner identity**:\n\n## Identity derivation (V2 region + tag mixed into all three identifiers)\n- **`LocalityResolver.identityRegion`** now prefixes the plain region with a fixed `\"V2\"` version tag (e.g. `\"V2NSW\"`). This region is the segment embedded inside the `memberId`, so the member id changes and never reproduces a v1 value.\n- **`IdentityKey.of`** mixes `\"V2\"` into the hashed identity fields, so the identity key changes. Duplicate detection is unaffected (every key gets the same tag, so equality is preserved).\n- **`HouseholdNormalizer.householdId`** mixes `\"V2\"` into the hashed household fields, so the household id changes while same-household owners still derive the identical value.\n\n## User-facing fields stay plain (no `V2`)\n- **`OwnerMapper.locality`** now derives the plain region directly from city/postcode (`LocalityResolver.resolve`) instead of reading it back from the member id's now-tagged REGION segment. So `locality` stays `\"NSW\"`, `timezone` maps correctly, and the `ownerSegment` area stays on the plain region.\n\n## Response shape\n- `openapi.yml`: added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema and grouped `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey` under a nested **`identity`** object; removed them from the top level; added a top-level integer **`apiVersion`** (2).\n- `OwnerMapper`: added `apiVersion` (constant 2) and an `identity(owner)` builder.\n\n## Audit event \u2192 schema version 2\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` now carries **`schemaVersion` = 2** and the **`ownerSegment`** recomputed from the version\u20112 identity: `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nThe request fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
