    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, from the moment the request arrives to the 201 response.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Framework-level, before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto`, triggered by `@Valid @RequestBody`). Any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** with a `ProblemDetail`. Constraints, per field:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters plus up to two space/apostrophe/hyphen-separated parts)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^\\+?[0-9 ()\\-]+$)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank) \u2014 all optional\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (email shape), `@Email` \u2014 optional\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Size(4..4)`, `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` \u2014 optional\n   - `title` \u2014 enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`; `registrationDate`/`birthDate` \u2014 ISO date `@Valid`\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Idempotency wrapper (`addOwner`)\n\n3. Read the `Idempotency-Key` header. If present and already seen, return the cached `OwnerDto` with **200 OK** (no new owner created). Otherwise fall through to `createOwner`, and cache the result under the key afterward.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 The `createOwner` pipeline (in this exact order)\n\n4. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; `id` and `pets` ignored).\n5. **Normalize + validate fields** (`normalizeOwnerFields`), sub-steps in order:\n   - a. **Normalize address** \u2014 trims/collapses/upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; prefers structured `addressLine1/2` over flat `address`; throws `InvalidAddressException` (**400**) if blank.\n   - b. **Normalize + validate telephone** to E.164 \u2014 strips to `+` and digits, requires 8\u201315 digits, and enforces national-number length by country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n   - c. **Lowercase email**.\n   - d. **Reject disposable-email domains** (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (**400**).\n   - e. **Validate postcode against city region** (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts anything) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n   - f. **Reject future registration date** \u2192 `InvalidRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n   - g. **Default the registration date** to today if absent, then **roll forward** off weekends/public holidays to the next business day.\n6. **Quota rejections** (`rejectDisallowedOwnerCreation`), in order:\n   - a. **Daily limit** \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already registered today \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n   - b. **City capacity** \u2014 if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (**409**).\n7. **Apply household membership** \u2014 sets `householdId` (SHA-256 over last name + postcode) and `householdSize`; captures whether the caller declared `sharesHousehold`.\n8. **Reject duplicate identity** \u2014 scans all existing (non-deleted) owners; if any shares the same identity key (SHA-256 over telephone + email + Soundex of last name) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n9. **Assign soft-duplicate flags** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` when another owner shares postcode + Soundex(last name) but a different identity key.\n10. **Assign derived fields** \u2014 `namesakeCount`, a unique `memberId` (Luhn/SHA-based, de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix against existing member IDs), plus `bulkSignupWarning` (\u2265 80/day) and `capacityWarning` (\u2265 40/city) flags.\n11. **Assign membership level** \u2014 household-capped level.\n12. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` inside `@Transactional`. **Entity-level Bean Validation fires at flush**: `@NotEmpty` on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`, and `@Pattern` E.164 on `telephone`.\n13. **Map** saved entity \u2192 `OwnerDto` response (computes display/derived fields).\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Side-effects after save\n\n14. **Audit log (human-readable)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: ...\")`.\n15. **Audit event (structured)** \u2014 serializes an immutable `OwnerCreatedEvent` record (with a global monotonic sequence number and schema version 2) to JSON on the `AUDIT` logger.\n16. **Welcome notification** \u2014 `NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome notification: ...\")` with owner ID + member ID.\n17. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- There are **no JPA lifecycle callbacks, no `@EntityListeners`, no Spring Data auditing, and no `ApplicationEventPublisher`**. Every \"event\"/side-effect above is done explicitly in the controller, and the audit/notify steps are just SLF4J log emissions \u2014 not durable, not transactional.\n- **Uniqueness is enforced in application code, not the database** \u2014 no `@Column(unique=...)` or unique index. The identity/member-ID/quota checks all scan `findAllOwners()`, and each `findAllOwners`/`saveOwner` runs in its own transaction (the controller pipeline is not itself transactional), so those checks are subject to race conditions under concurrency.\n- The idempotency cache and the `OWNER_CREATED_SEQUENCE` are **in-memory only**, so they don't survive a restart or work across instances."
